Our Technical Architect has designed an architecture that deploys our AI/ML stack on a sovereign cloud infrastructure within the EU, such as Outscale or OVHcloud, using containerization with Docker and Kubernetes for scalability and reliability. We will implement API integration using our existing expertise in API gateways and standards, ensuring seamless authentication and authorization through our experience with identity providers. To meet the high availability requirement, we will design a highly available architecture with load balancing, auto-scaling, and monitoring using tools like Prometheus, Grafana, and ELK stack.

Our solution will provide assistance with consultation of information, drafting of administrative contents, instruction of files, and collaboration between agents and services. The Regulatory document Q&A assistant, similar to the one delivered in the public administration domain, can be adapted for search and information retrieval tasks, leveraging our RAG capabilities to provide relevant information. For drafting letters or answers, our language models such as Mistral 7B Instruct can be fine-tuned on a corpus of municipal documents to generate coherent and contextually appropriate text.

To ensure transparency and trust in the AI-driven decision-making process, we will implement explainability methods such as source citation (RAG grounding), chain-of-thought display, or confidence scoring. Our ai_security_controls include output PII redaction and confidence threshold escalation, ensuring that sensitive information is protected and decisions based on AI outputs are subject to review.

Our company is committed to strict GDPR compliance, hosting all data exclusively within the EU, adhering to a cross-border transfer policy that prohibits data transfers outside the EU by default, and utilizing anonymisation tools such as Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom NER models. Our model update security review process guarantees that no decision can be automated without explicit validation by an agent.

We are aware of the regulatory risks associated with AI solutions and have experience with GDPR compliance, including the presence of a Data Protection Agreement template version 3.2 and knowledge of standard legal basis for data processing under Article 6(1)(e) of the GDPR. Our no_automated_decision_without_human_validation_policy directly addresses the client's expectation that the tool should not supersede human decision-making.

Our green hosting partners, such as OVHcloud and Scaleway, both located in France and powered by 100% renewable energy, will help reduce energy consumption. We estimate that our solution can typically reduce energy consumption by 35% compared to the baseline. Our digital sobriety practices, including INT8/INT4 model quantisation, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching, and a green IT hardware procurement policy with a minimum 5-year lifecycle, will further contribute to lowering energy consumption.

The project will be managed using established methodologies, specifically PRINCE2 or Agile Scrum, given their suitability for public sector IT projects. We will leverage past public sector references, such as the digital workplace transformation for Comune di Torino and the AI-powered document management system for Regione Lombardia, to provide valuable insights into similar project challenges and best practices.

Our available capacity, with 60% of project management capacity available as of the reference year, can accommodate the City of Belval project without overcommitting our resources. The next available start date for new projects is March 1, 2025. We will implement a typical delivery structure phases (Inception & Design, Pilot / MVP, Full Rollout, Operations & Support) and utilize governance tools such as RAID logs, decision logs, change request processes, and steering committees to facilitate structured project management.

The proposed budget for the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years. Our pricing model includes standard daily rates for various roles and a target gross margin percentage of 28 percent. We will propose an approach allowing to optimize costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected.

In conclusion, our consortium proposes a comprehensive AI solution that meets the City of Belval's requirements, ensuring regulatory compliance, environmental sustainability, and effective project management. Our team is committed to delivering a high-quality solution that enhances the efficiency and effectiveness of municipal agents in their daily missions.
